<p id="A2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">when <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\ldots,z_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\ldots,z_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> are non-zero and distinct. In
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cule et al. (2008b)</a></cite>, it is shown that the required formula is</p>
